From: Slashy <amirramy.chatbi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:19:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(p01): the inference router tier follows the
 free-inference rule too

The loop computed a second, credits-only tier for model routing, so the agent
kept routing at tier critical with a free pool. Confirmed in production logs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NptGK4Xppd57AQrT6DuM24
---
 src/agent/loop.ts | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/agent/loop.ts b/src/agent/loop.ts
index 5c426fe..1e726f3 100644
--- a/src/agent/loop.ts
+++ b/src/agent/loop.ts
@@ -597,7 +597,9 @@ export async function runAgentLoop(
       pendingInput = undefined;
 
       // ── Inference Call (via router when available) ──
-      const survivalTier = getSurvivalTier(financial.creditsCents);
+      // p01: the tier that drives model routing must follow the same rule as
+      // the rest of the runtime — free inference is not a reason to throttle.
+      const survivalTier = getEffectiveSurvivalTier(config, financial.creditsCents, financial.usdcBalance);
       log(config, `[THINK] Routing inference (tier: ${survivalTier}, model: ${inference.getDefaultModel()})...`);
 
       const inferenceTools = toolsToInferenceFormat(tools);
